@startuml
title Secure Node Registration & Telemetry Ingestion Pipeline

actor Agent
participant "Nginx Gateway" as Nginx
participant "Ingestion Worker" as Worker
participant "Local CA" as LocalCA
database Redis
queue Redpanda
participant Vector
database ClickHouse
actor Administrator as Admin

note over Agent
Initial State
- No client certificate
- No trusted agent_id
- Collect hostname, device type,
  and hardware fingerprint
end note

== Phase 1: Node Bootstrap Registration ==

Agent -> Nginx: RegisterNode()\nTLS + bootstrap_token + hardware_info
activate Nginx

Nginx -> Worker: Forward registration request
activate Worker

Worker -> Worker: Validate bootstrap token\n(Constant-time verification)

alt Invalid bootstrap token

    Worker --> Nginx: Registration failed
    Nginx --> Agent: Registration rejected

else Valid bootstrap token

    Worker -> Worker: Generate new agent_id\nDefault state = DISCOVERED / UNASSIGNED

    Worker -> LocalCA: GenerateCredentials(agent_id)
    activate LocalCA
    LocalCA --> Worker: X.509 certificate + private key
    deactivate LocalCA

    Worker -> Redis: Persist node registry\nnode:agent:<agent_id>\nAdd agent_id to index
    activate Redis
    Redis --> Worker: OK
    deactivate Redis

    Worker --> Nginx: RegisterNodeResponse\nagent_id + certificate + private key
    Nginx --> Agent: Registration successful

end

deactivate Worker
deactivate Nginx

note over Agent
Persist certificate and private key locally.

All subsequent communication
uses mutual TLS (mTLS).
end note

== Phase 1.5: Administrative Node Assignment ==

Admin -> Redis: Query DISCOVERED / UNASSIGNED nodes
activate Redis
Redis --> Admin: Node inventory
deactivate Redis

Admin -> Redis: Assign operational metadata\nState -> ASSIGNED / ACTIVE\nRack / Site / Labels
activate Redis
Redis --> Admin: OK
deactivate Redis

== Phase 2: Telemetry Ingestion ==

loop Periodic telemetry upload

    Agent -> Nginx: mTLS + IngestBatch(metrics[])
    activate Nginx

    alt Client certificate invalid

        Nginx --> Agent: TLS handshake rejected

    else Client certificate valid

        Nginx -> Nginx: Extract client certificate DN

        Nginx -> Worker: Forward telemetry batch\n+ client certificate DN
        activate Worker

        Worker -> Worker: Extract agent_id\nfrom certificate DN

        Worker -> Redis: Lookup node by agent_id
        activate Redis
        Redis --> Worker: Node status + assignment
        deactivate Redis

        alt Node not found\nUNASSIGNED\nor RETIRED

            Worker --> Nginx: Reject telemetry
            Nginx --> Agent: Ingestion rejected

        else Authorized node

            Worker -> Worker: Build telemetry envelope\nEnvelopeID\nAgentID\nReceivedAt\nClientDN\nPayload

            Worker -> Redpanda: Publish\ntelemetry.ingested-raw.received
            activate Redpanda
            Redpanda --> Worker: ACK
            deactivate Redpanda

            Worker --> Nginx: accepted = true
            Nginx --> Agent: Batch accepted

        end

        deactivate Worker

    end

    deactivate Nginx

end

== Phase 3: Normalization & Storage ==

Vector -> Redpanda: Consume telemetry.ingested-raw.received

activate Redpanda
Redpanda --> Vector: Raw telemetry envelope
deactivate Redpanda

activate Vector

Vector -> Vector: Normalize payload\n- batch_sequence\n- agent_id\n- received_at\n- hardware_fingerprint\n- metrics[]

Vector -> Redpanda: Publish\ntelemetry.normalized.received

activate Redpanda
Redpanda --> Vector: ACK
deactivate Redpanda

deactivate Vector

Redpanda -> ClickHouse: Stream normalized telemetry

activate ClickHouse

ClickHouse -> ClickHouse: Materialized Views\nFlatten metrics[]\nPopulate telemetry tables\nRefresh serving views

deactivate ClickHouse

== Design Notes ==

note over Worker,Redis
Telemetry is accepted only for
nodes that exist in the registry
and are operationally assigned.
end note

note over Vector,ClickHouse
Vector performs normalization only.

ClickHouse stores the structured
historical telemetry and provides
optimized analytical views.
end note
@enduml